{"type":"api-request-blob","sessionId":"8712e5cb-5c17-4f78-8159-fe8e322bd52d","hash":"cd46cd51289d01d0620974131c1dafa7936d64a21e2716cefcae7b4807ecd7e3","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_019eZBguJg758fnTugq2B4Yb","name":"Edit","input":{"file_path":"/Users/vojta/Dev/protocodus.github.io/.claude/worktrees/hedgerow/fun/hedgerow/README.md","old_string":"    `effects.js` (particles), `atmosphere.js` (halos, mist, decals),","new_string":"    `effects.js` (particles: smoke and dust lit by the nearest lamps,\n    fires and flashes, soft where they meet the scene; blasts throw up a\n    column of earth and roll dust along the ground), `atmosphere.js`\n    (halos, mist, decals),"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01H2rCNo9fzBwPai2NnPmfnU","name":"Edit","input":{"file_path":"/Users/vojta/Dev/protocodus.github.io/.claude/worktrees/hedgerow/fun/hedgerow/README.md","old_string":"  * the effects chain (`renderer.setEffects`, in order): `ssao.js` ambient","new_string":"  * the effects chain (`renderer.setEffects`, in order): the particles of\n    `effects.js` drawn into the scene's buffer with its depth · `ssao.js` ambient"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01Uo3NGJXP7u8wHGDcnYdwcf","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /Users/vojta/Dev/protocodus.github.io/.claude/worktrees/hedgerow && git status --short fun/hedgerow && git add fun/hedgerow/js/effects.js fun/hedgerow/js/main.js fun/hedgerow/README.md && git commit -q -F - <<'EOF'\nHedgerow graphics: lit, soft combat smoke and fuller blasts\n\nSmoke, dust and spray now take the light of the eight lamps, fires and\nflashes the light pool picks (relative to the night's ambient, soft-capped\nso smoke beside a blast glows rather than clipping), so a burning truck\nlights its smoke from below and gun smoke flares with the shot. With the\neffects chain the particles are drawn into the scene's buffer first and\nread its depth: they fade out where they meet walls and the ground (no\nhard lines), and the occlusion, reflections and glow passes treat them as\npart of the scene. Low quality keeps drawing them with the scene.\n\nThe atlas is twice the resolution, with smoke built from warped noise and\nflames broken into licks; grenades and charges throw up a column of earth\n(or water) and roll dust along the ground; wet ground spits water with\nthe dirt when hit; impact sparks are thinner streaks.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nEOF\ngit log --oneline -1","description":"Commit round 7, the combat effects"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}]}}
