{"parentUuid":"5551c226-1011-41cd-934f-cf3404e8dc55","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgFQNKfZxpbfKZQsvJYT4","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"**Hedgerow vegetation round: GPU meadow grass**\nThis moves the grass round (wire in, tune, verify, commit) into its own session, starting from this branch tip."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5355,"cache_read_input_tokens":562198,"output_tokens":1452,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":110},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":5355,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1452,"cache_read_input_tokens":562198,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5355,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":5355},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"f56947ab-3f25-43b8-ad60-0e5cea87c3fa","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CgFQNJgHXPPuaANhiUWPw","requestRef":"3c96f6bf-dc75-40d6-8f74-c9fef02d45d1","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"16dc9ec0-4a10-4d41-a81e-5c705ee99bcc","timestamp":"2026-10-21T12:44:41.864Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"max","perTurnEffort":"max","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/vojta/Dev/protocodus.github.io/.claude/worktrees/hedgerow","sessionId":"8712e5cb-5c17-4f78-8159-fe8e322bd52d","version":"2.1.304","gitBranch":"hedgerow-poc","slug":"shimmying-swimming-falcon"}
{"parentUuid":"16dc9ec0-4a10-4d41-a81e-5c705ee99bcc","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgFQNKfZxpbfKZQsvJYT4","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01G1GU1rGFKCSzwZMbMPoUZc","name":"mcp__ccd_session__hand_off_to_session","input":{"title":"Hedgerow vegetation round: GPU meadow grass","remaining_plan":"Finish the vegetation round of the Hedgerow graphics goal (\"constantly and iteratively improve the game graphics towards AAA (Call of Duty, Medal of Honor); commit each improvement\"; commit only, never push). Game: fun/hedgerow in this repo (three.js r185, no build).\n\nState: fun/hedgerow/js/grass.js is committed (7884f6b6) but NOT wired in. It exports createGrass({ terrain, world, level, shared, n = 256, spacing = 0.16 }) → { mesh, update(camera, playerPos), setCount(n), uniforms }. It is one instanced draw of single blades on a camera-snapped grid of world cells. Each blade's data comes from an integer hash of its cell; the ground height and density come from a half-float RG DataTexture built at load from terrain.grid (H), level.splat weights, slope and the water level, with MOVE colliders' footprints cut out. It adds wind gust waves and parts the grass round the player. It patches a MeshStandardMaterial via onBeforeCompile (vertex position in beginnormal/begin_vertex, colour in color_fragment, faceDirection forced to 1). Untested: it may have GLSL errors (it uses gl_InstanceID and uint hashing, so it needs WebGL2 GLSL3).\n\nTo do:\n1. Wire it in. config.js QUALITY gets a blades count (high 256, medium 192, low 0). main.js creates it after the level is built (G.terrain, G.world, G.level, G.shared), adds the mesh to the scene, and calls grass.update(camera, G.player?.pos) every frame. applyGraphics → setCount(quality.blades).\n2. Verify in the built-in browser (the pane is usually hidden; don't force it visible). Serve your own worktree with the scratch server (POST /__snap/<name> saves JPEGs to its snaps/ folder) on a port other than 8765. That port is this session's server, serving the old worktree. Add your own entry to /Users/vojta/Dev/protocodus.github.io/.claude/launch.json, and don't touch the main checkout's files otherwise. Server script: python3 -I REDACTED.py <port> <worktree root>. Capture frames with canvas toDataURL after G.renderer.render, using hedgerow.flyTo views. Good grass views: field go(-24, 34, 0.6, -0.08), lane banks z 0..80, river meadow near z 255, forest clearing. Check there's no grass on roads, in houses or in the river; check the blade look at night, wind, the patch-edge fade and performance; tune colours and density.\n3. Optionally improve the other vegetation (the CPU scattered cover is in levels/saint-clair.js; vegetation.js has the LODs).\n4. Update README.md (the \"How it is built\" list and the look paragraph). Run node tests (world-check, lod-check, distance-check, ai-check), then commit as \"Hedgerow graphics: …\" with the Co-Authored-By line.\n5. When done: stop your server, close your browser tab, and remove your launch.json entry (needs dangerouslyDisableSandbox).\n\nDon't touch camera.js, player.js, hud.js or character.js. The original session is converting the game to first person in them, on branch hedgerow-poc. Never commit Blender preview renders."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5355,"cache_read_input_tokens":562198,"output_tokens":1452,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":110},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":5355,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1452,"cache_read_input_tokens":562198,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5355,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":5355},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01G1GU1rGFKCSzwZMbMPoUZc":{"title":"Hedgerow vegetation round: GPU meadow grass","remaining_plan":"Finish the vegetation round of the Hedgerow graphics goal (\"constantly and iteratively improve the game graphics towards AAA (Call of Duty, Medal of Honor); commit each improvement\"; commit only, never push). Game: fun/hedgerow in this repo (three.js r185, no build).\n\nState: fun/hedgerow/js/grass.js is committed (7884f6b6) but NOT wired in. It exports createGrass({ terrain, world, level, shared, n = 256, spacing = 0.16 }) → { mesh, update(camera, playerPos), setCount(n), uniforms }. It is one instanced draw of single blades on a camera-snapped grid of world cells. Each blade's data comes from an integer hash of its cell; the ground height and density come from a half-float RG DataTexture built at load from terrain.grid (H), level.splat weights, slope and the water level, with MOVE colliders' footprints cut out. It adds wind gust waves and parts the grass round the player. It patches a MeshStandardMaterial via onBeforeCompile (vertex position in beginnormal/begin_vertex, colour in color_fragment, faceDirection forced to 1). Untested: it may have GLSL errors (it uses gl_InstanceID and uint hashing, so it needs WebGL2 GLSL3).\n\nTo do:\n1. Wire it in. config.js QUALITY gets a blades count (high 256, medium 192, low 0). main.js creates it after the level is built (G.terrain, G.world, G.level, G.shared), adds the mesh to the scene, and calls grass.update(camera, G.player?.pos) every frame. applyGraphics → setCount(quality.blades).\n2. Verify in the built-in browser (the pane is usually hidden; don't force it visible). Serve your own worktree with the scratch server (POST /__snap/<name> saves JPEGs to its snaps/ folder) on a port other than 8765. That port is this session's server, serving the old worktree. Add your own entry to /Users/vojta/Dev/protocodus.github.io/.claude/launch.json, and don't touch the main checkout's files otherwise. Server script: python3 -I REDACTED.py <port> <worktree root>. Capture frames with canvas toDataURL after G.renderer.render, using hedgerow.flyTo views. Good grass views: field go(-24, 34, 0.6, -0.08), lane banks z 0..80, river meadow near z 255, forest clearing. Check there's no grass on roads, in houses or in the river; check the blade look at night, wind, the patch-edge fade and performance; tune colours and density.\n3. Optionally improve the other vegetation (the CPU scattered cover is in levels/saint-clair.js; vegetation.js has the LODs).\n4. Update README.md (the \"How it is built\" list and the look paragraph). Run node tests (world-check, lod-check, distance-check, ai-check), then commit as \"Hedgerow graphics: …\" with the Co-Authored-By line.\n5. When done: stop your server, close your browser tab, and remove your launch.json entry (needs dangerouslyDisableSandbox).\n\nDon't touch camera.js, player.js, hud.js or character.js. The original session is converting the game to first person in them, on branch hedgerow-poc. Never commit Blender preview renders."}},"serverClassifierRequest":"f56947ab-3f25-43b8-ad60-0e5cea87c3fa","apiBlockIndex":2,"requestId":"req_011CgFQNJgHXPPuaANhiUWPw","requestRef":"3c96f6bf-dc75-40d6-8f74-c9fef02d45d1","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"c5b4c34e-a846-4b30-826f-e1b1e099dbd5","timestamp":"2026-10-21T12:44:53.260Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"max","perTurnEffort":"max","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/vojta/Dev/protocodus.github.io/.claude/worktrees/hedgerow","sessionId":"8712e5cb-5c17-4f78-8159-fe8e322bd52d","version":"2.1.304","gitBranch":"hedgerow-poc","slug":"shimmying-swimming-falcon"}
