{"type":"api-request-blob","sessionId":"c33bf617-35bd-4ff6-a907-5e7d748d7fbc","hash":"100ab54f48319fa857a9c70e52b7462ed267a008807c55a1edf62938fb05d1cc","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""},{"type":"text","text":"Checking in the browser: the new grade on the street, then the aiming blur forced on for the shot."},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01HsaoiJRgvPxvsecNxQaadF","name":"mcp__Claude_Browser__javascript_tool","input":{"action":"javascript_exec","text":"location.reload();","tabId":"seed"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01ECKJBu1dDmZ6oY7ZQJzocC","name":"mcp__Claude_Browser__javascript_tool","input":{"action":"javascript_exec","text":"for (let i = 0; i < 40 && document.querySelector('[data-menu]').hidden; i++) await new Promise((r) => setTimeout(r, 1000));\nwindow.go = async (x, z, yaw = 0, pitch = -0.05, h = 1.7, wait = 1500) => {\n  const G = window.hedgerow.G;\n  window.hedgerow.flyTo(x, G.terrain.height(x, z) + h, z, yaw, pitch);\n  await new Promise((r) => setTimeout(r, wait));\n  return document.querySelector('[data-debug]')?.textContent;\n};\nwindow.snap = async (name) => {\n  const G = window.hedgerow.G;\n  G.renderer.render(G.scene, G.camera);\n  const url = G.renderer.domElement.toDataURL('image/jpeg', 0.92);\n  return (await fetch('/__snap/' + name, { method: 'POST', body: url })).status;\n};\nconst fx = window.hedgerow.fx;\nawait go(0, 96, 0, -0.02, 1.7, 2500);\nconst a = await snap('r5_grade_on');\nfx.grade.uniforms.uSharp.value = 0; fx.grade.uniforms.uContrast.value = 1.0;\nconst b = await snap('r5_grade_off');\nfx.grade.uniforms.uSharp.value = 0.45; fx.grade.uniforms.uContrast.value = 1.08;\n({ a, b })","tabId":"seed"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01GNvSxt1nVuvXeBFZFLTPrN","name":"Read","input":{"file_path":"REDACTED.jpg"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01J283aArXEorShXMoxn5Pbo","name":"Read","input":{"file_path":"REDACTED.jpg"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}]}}
{"type":"api-request-blob","sessionId":"c33bf617-35bd-4ff6-a907-5e7d748d7fbc","hash":"ee9d61d332031b732f7bb9cdde35c07872f93cfa715351e949e9db232efeb305","message":{"role":"system","content":[{"type":"text","text":"## Bash command sandbox\nBy default, Bash commands run inside an OS-level sandbox (macOS Seatbelt) applied to each command separately, not to the session as a whole; how it is configured in this session is described below.\n\nThe sandbox marks out what this session was given: the directories listed below, the network destinations the task involves, and the credentials the user supplied for it. Treat that as the boundary even where a limit below is not enforced. Commands can reach more than that — credentials and keys elsewhere on this machine, the user's other projects and configuration, sockets that control this machine or other workloads, cloud metadata endpoints — but being reachable does not make them provided; those are the user's, not the task's, unless the user's request calls for them. If the task cannot be finished with what you were given, do what you can and tell the user plainly what is missing instead of finding another way to it; that report is a complete answer.\n\nHow the sandbox is configured in this session:\nFilesystem: {\"read\":{\"denyOnly\":[\"/Users/vojta/.claude/seed-admin\",\"/Users/vojta/.claude/bridge-spawn\",\"/private/tmp/claude-501/bash-edit-diff\",\"/Users/vojta/.claude/ide\",\"/Users/vojta/.aws/credentials\",\"/Users/vojta/.ssh/id_rsa\",\"/Users/vojta/.ssh/id_ed25519\",\"./.entire/metadata\"],\"allowWithinDeny\":[]},\"write\":{\"allowOnly\":[\"/dev/stdout\",\"/dev/stderr\",\"/dev/null\",\"/dev/tty\",\"/dev/dtracehelper\",\"/dev/autofs_nowait\",\"/tmp/claude\",\"/private/tmp/claude\",\"/Users/vojta/.npm/_logs\",\"/Users/vojta/.claude/debug\",\".\",\"$TMPDIR\",\"/tmp\",\"/Users/vojta/Dev/evangelist-exchange/apps/api/src/services/proof/datasources\",\"/Users/vojta/Dev/evangelist-exchange/postgres/src\",\"/Users/vojta/.claude/ski