{"type":"api-request-blob","sessionId":"c33bf617-35bd-4ff6-a907-5e7d748d7fbc","hash":"dbd0641bd6cbeeed1bc890db208a52a7dcecfd92319bbd68be6daa5418072996","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""},{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I'll integrate this in four spots—quality presets, post-level-build creation, a per-frame update alongside vegetation, and the quality switch—allocating upfront for the high-quality maximum since `setCount` can't expand the dummy instanced attribute later.\n\n","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01Wk8LRNjz9HqUvT1CF7ahoe","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /Users/vojta/Dev/protocodus.github.io/.claude/worktrees/hedgerow-grass/fun/hedgerow && python3 - <<'PYEOF'\np = 'js/grass.js'\ns = open(p).read()\nold = \"\"\"export function createGrass({ terrain, world, level, shared, n = 256, spacing = 0.16 }) {\"\"\"\nnew = \"\"\"export function createGrass({ terrain, world, level, shared, n = 256, max = 256, spacing = 0.16 }) {\"\"\"\nassert old in s; s = s.replace(old, new)\nold = \"\"\"  // three draws as many instances as its instanced attributes allow: one dummy\n  geo.setAttribute('aCell', new THREE.InstancedBufferAttribute(new Float32Array(n * n), 1));\n  geo.instanceCount = n * n;\"\"\"\nnew = \"\"\"  // three draws as many instances as its instanced attributes allow: one dummy, for the most\n  geo.setAttribute('aCell', new THREE.InstancedBufferAttribute(new Float32Array(max * max), 1));\n  geo.instanceCount = n * n;\"\"\"\nassert old in s; s = s.replace(old, new)\nold = \"\"\"  const mesh = new THREE.Mesh(geo, mat);\n  mesh.name = 'grass';\n  mesh.frustumCulled = false;\"\"\"\nnew = \"\"\"  const mesh = new THREE.Mesh(geo, mat);\n  mesh.name = 'grass';\n  mesh.visible = n > 0;\n  mesh.frustumCulled = false;\"\"\"\nassert old in s; s = s.replace(old, new)\nold = \"\"\"    setCount(m) {\n      n = m;\"\"\"\nnew = \"\"\"    setCount(m) {\n      n = Math.min(m, max);\n      m = n;\"\"\"\nassert old in s; s = s.replace(old, new)\nopen(p, 'w').write(s)\n\np = 'js/config.js'\ns = open(p).read()\nfor q, b in (('high', 256), ('medium', 192), ('low', 0)):\n    i = s.index(f'  {q}: {{')\n    j = s.index('treeNear', i)\n    s = s[:j] + f'blades: {b}, ' + s[j:]\nopen(p, 'w').write(s)\n\np = 'js/main.js'\ns = open(p).read()\nold = \"import { createSSR } from './ssr.js';\"\nnew = \"import { createSSR } from './ssr.js';\\nimport { createGrass } from './grass.js';\"\nassert old in s; s = s.replace(old, new)\nold = \"\"\"  built = buildLevel(G, LEVEL, quality);\n  G.cover = built.cover;\n  G.effects.setGround((x, z) => G.terrain.height(x, z));\"\"\"\nnew = \"\"\"  built = buildLevel(G, LEVEL, quality);\n  G.cover = built.cover;\n  G.effects.setGround((x, z) => G.terrain.height(x, z));\n  // the meadow grass, blade by blade round the camera\n  G.grass = createGrass({ terrain: G.terrain, world: G.world, level: LEVEL, shared, n: quality.blades ?? 0 });\n  scene.add(G.grass.mesh);\"\"\"\nassert old in s; s = s.replace(old, new)\nold = \"\"\"  G?.weather?.setCount(quality.rain);\"\"\"\nnew = \"\"\"  G?.weather?.setCount(quality.rain);\n  G?.grass?.setCount(quality.blades ?? 0);\"\"\"\nassert old in s; s = s.replace(old, new)\nold = \"\"\"  built.veg.update(dt, camera, quality);\"\"\"\nnew = \"\"\"  built.veg.update(dt, camera, quality);\n  G.grass.update(camera, player?.pos);\"\"\"\nassert old in s; s = s.replace(old, new)\nopen(p, 'w').write(s)\nprint('ok')\nPYEOF\ngrep -n \"blades\" js/config.js; for f in js/grass.js js/main.js js/config.js; do node --check $f || echo FAIL; done; echo checked","description":"Wire the grass into quality presets and main"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}]}}
