{"parentUuid":"6e6afb4f-c6e5-46e3-98ff-5a8793299382","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"edited_text_file","filename":"/Users/vojta/Dev/protocodus.github.io/.claude/worktrees/hedgerow/fun/hedgerow/js/dof.js","snippet":"3\t   A pass for `renderer.setEffects`, after the light in the rain and\n4\t   before the bloom (so the bloom of a soft lamp is soft too). While the soldier\n5\t   aims down his sights the background beyond the point under the\n6\t   crosshair goes soft, more the further it lies behind it (focus\n7\t   pulling, as a camera lens or the eye does); what is at the focus and in\n8\t   front of it stays sharp. The depth comes from the scene pass of the same\n9\t   frame (the first passes of the chain see it; this one borrows it). A\n10\t   16-tap golden-angle disc, each tap weighted by its own blur so a sharp\n11\t   soldier in front does not smear into the soft hedge behind him. The\n12\t   focus looks past the rifle itself (first person, its front sight is\n13\t   under the crosshair), and what is right at the eye — the rear sight, the\n14\t   hands — goes a little soft too, as a real peep sight does. Off (and free)\n15\t   when not aiming. */\n16\t\n17\timport * as THREE from 'three';\n18\t\n19\tconst VERT = /* glsl */ `\n20\tvarying vec2 vUv;\n21\tvoid main() { vUv = uv; gl_Position = vec4(position.xy, 0.0, 1.0); }`;\n22\t\n23\tconst FRAG = /* glsl */ `\n24\tuniform sampler2D tSrc, tDepth;\n25\tuniform mat4 uProjInv;\n26\tuniform float uAim, uMaxPx, uNearPx;\n27\tuniform vec2 uTexel;\n28\tvarying vec2 vUv;\n29\t\n30\tfloat dist(vec2 uv) {\n31\t  float d = texture2D(tDepth, uv).x;\n32\t  if (d >= 1.0) return 1e4;\n33\t  vec4 v = uProjInv * vec4(uv * 2.0 - 1.0, d * 2.0 - 1.0, 1.0);\n34\t  return length(v.xyz / v.w);\n35\t}\n36\t// blur in pixels for a point at distance d with the focus at f\n37\tfloat coc(float d, float f) {\n38\t  float far = clamp((d - f) / max(d, 1e-3) * 1.25, 0.0, 1.0) * uMaxPx;\n39\t  float near = (1.0 - smoothstep(0.18, 0.45, d)) * uNearPx;\n40\t  return max(far, near) * uAim;\n41\t}\n42\t// a focus tap: past the rifle (nearer than 1.2 m is the gun itself)\n43\tfloat focusAt(vec2 uv) { float d = dist(uv); return d < 1.2 ? 1e4 : d; }\n44\t\n45\tvoid main() {\n46\t  // the focus: what lies under the crosshair (a few taps, the nearest wins)\n47\t  float f = min(min(focusAt(vec2(0.5)), focusAt(vec2(0.5) + uTexel * vec2(6.0, 0.0))), focusAt(vec2(0.5) - uTexel * vec2(6.0, 0.0)));\n48\t  f = max(f, 2.0);\n49\t  vec3 c0 = texture2D(tSrc, vUv).rgb;\n50\t  float r0 = coc(dist(vUv), f);\n51\t  if (r0 < 0.5) { gl_FragColor = vec4(c0, 1.0); return; }\n52\t  vec3 sum = c0;\n53\t  float wsum = 1.0;\n54\t  for (int i = 0; i < 16; i++) {\n55\t    float t = (float(i) + 0.5) / 16.0;\n...\n58\texport function createDOF(camera) {\n59\t  const geometry = new THREE.BufferGeometry();\n60\t  geometry.setAttribute('position', new THREE.Float32BufferAttribute([-1, 3, 0, -1, -1, 0, 3, -1, 0], 3));\n61\t  geometry.setAttribute('uv', new THREE.Float32BufferAttribute([0, 2, 0, 0, 2, 0], 2));\n62\t  const material = new THREE.ShaderMaterial({\n63\t    vertexShader: VERT, fragmentShader: FRAG,\n64\t    uniforms: {\n65\t      tSrc: { value: null }, tDepth: { value: null }, uProjInv: { value: new THREE.Matrix4() },\n66\t      uAim: { value: 0 }, uMaxPx: { value: 7 }, uNearPx: { value: 3 }, uTexel: { value: new THREE.Vector2(1 / 1024, 1 / 768) },\n67\t    },\n68\t    depthTest: false, depthWrite: false, toneMapped: false,\n69\t  });\n70\t  const quad = new THREE.Mesh(geometry, material);\n71\t  quad.frustumCulled = false;\n72\t  const ortho = new THREE.OrthographicCamera(-1, 1, 1, -1, 0, 1);\n73\t  const u = material.uniforms;\n74\t  let depth = null;\n...\n78\t    set(depthTexture, aim) {\n79\t      depth = depthTexture;\n80\t      u.uAim.value = aim;\n81\t      this.enabled = !!depthTexture && aim > 0.02;\n82\t    },\n83\t    setSize(w, h) {\n84\t      u.uTexel.value.set(1 / w, 1 / h);\n85\t      u.uMaxPx.value = 5 * h / 768;\n86\t      u.uNearPx.value = 3 * h / 768;\n87\t    },\n88\t    render(renderer, writeBuffer, readBuffer) {\n89\t      u.uProjInv.value.copy(camera.projectionMatrixInverse);\n90\t      u.tSrc.value = readBuffer.texture;\n91\t      u.tDepth.value = depth;\n92\t      renderer.setRenderTarget(writeBuffer);\n93\t      renderer.render(quad, ortho);\n94\t    },"},"type":"attachment","uuid":"52038a17-2e8b-4407-b7de-e806c45b4778","timestamp":"2026-10-21T12:53:57.141Z","rendered":[{"content":"<system-reminder>\nNote: /Users/vojta/Dev/protocodus.github.io/.claude/worktrees/hedgerow/fun/hedgerow/js/dof.js changed on disk since you last read it. That's usually deliberate, so take it as the current state rather than reverting it; if the change looks wrong, say so rather than undoing it yourself — otherwise no need to call it out. Here are the relevant changes (shown with line numbers):\n3\t   A pass for `renderer.setEffects`, after the light in the rain and\n4\t   before the bloom (so the bloom of a soft lamp is soft too). While the soldier\n5\t   aims down his sights the background beyond the point under the\n6\t   crosshair goes soft, more the further it lies behind it (focus\n7\t   pulling, as a camera lens or the eye does); what is at the focus and in\n8\t   front of it stays sharp. The depth comes from the scene pass of the same\n9\t   frame (the first passes of the chain see it; this one borrows it). A\n10\t   16-tap golden-angle disc, each tap weighted by its own blur so a sharp\n11\t   soldier in front does not smear into the soft hedge behind him. The\n12\t   focus looks past the rifle itself (first person, its front sight is\n13\t   under the crosshair), and what is right at the eye — the rear sight, the\n14\t   hands — goes a little soft too, as a real peep sight does. Off (and free)\n15\t   when not aiming. */\n16\t\n17\timport * as THREE from 'three';\n18\t\n19\tconst VERT = /* glsl */ `\n20\tvarying vec2 vUv;\n21\tvoid main() { vUv = uv; gl_Position = vec4(pos