{"type":"api-request-blob","sessionId":"c33bf617-35bd-4ff6-a907-5e7d748d7fbc","hash":"22896e17279f0e38413f95f07bc04b121f09eadc8aefbb1f7bd2275252486546","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01K1CWsuHzZ4e5HPjf1rNiYN","name":"Edit","input":{"file_path":"/Users/vojta/Dev/protocodus.github.io/.claude/worktrees/hedgerow-grass/fun/hedgerow/README.md","old_string":"    the level, open towards the far buildings) and the next village","new_string":"    the level, open towards the far buildings) and the next village\n  * `grass.js` the meadow grass on the GPU: one instanced draw of tufts of\n    blades round the camera (high ~21 m, medium ~14 m, none on low), each\n    placed, sized and leaned by a hash of its world cell, on a ground map\n    made at load from the terrain's own splat (none on roads, mud, steep\n    banks, at the water or inside anything solid); the ground under it\n    turns to dark, dry sward"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_0114TV6ghonGF6cTx43iaiF1","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /Users/vojta/Dev/protocodus.github.io/.claude/worktrees/hedgerow-grass && git add fun/hedgerow/README.md && git commit -q -m \"Hedgerow: grass.js gets its own line in the README\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\" && git log --oneline -3 && git merge-tree --write-tree --name-only hedgerow-poc hedgerow-grass; echo \"merge-tree exit: $?\"","description":"Commit the README move and re-check the trial merge"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}]}}
