{"parentUuid":"cbfded87-7c21-49fe-b6e7-826144b9956d","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgFSDnS86MvKdAHkPd2M9","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I finished the meadow grass and committed it on branch `refs/heads/hedgerow-grass` (030eece3, plus 3805bf70 for the README). Nothing is pushed. It isn't on `hedgerow-poc` yet: a trial merge into your current tip, the first-person commit 7e251d81, has no conflicts, and the merged `main.js` parses with the wiring intact. Merging is yours to do.\n\n**What it is:** the meadows and verges are now tufts of five thin blades drawn round the camera. Each blade bends in the wind (gusts roll across the field) and gives way round the player's legs. Far tufts thin out and the patch fades at its edge, with no visible ring. The ground under the grass turns dark and rough, with no puddles. Quality presets: high draws 192 × 192 tufts out to about 21 m, medium 128 × 128 to about 14 m, low none.\n\n**Checked in the browser:**\n- No grass on roads, the square, track centres, underwater ground, steep banks, or inside anything solid.\n- Thin posts, planks and sandbag walls also clear the grass around them.\n- Two lids sitting 4–10 cm above the ground still have grass over them, which looks natural.\n- Low quality starts without errors and leaves the ground untouched.\n- The four node tests pass.\n\n**Cost:** about 1–1.5 ms per frame in an open meadow at 1024×768 on the M1 Max. That's measured by alternating grass on and off, because single readings in the hidden pane were noisy. Expect roughly double at high's 1.5 pixel ratio, which dynamic resolution should absorb.\n\n**Fixes along the way:**\n- The first version's single blades read as black spikes on bright ground, so I rebuilt them as tufts and lightened the colours.\n- Strongly leaned blades stretched into long streaks; they now bend along an arc that keeps their length.\n- Building the grass map took 4.3 s of loading. It now reuses the terrain mesh's own surface weights and takes 0.1 s.\n\n**For your merge:** my changes touch `README.md`, `config.js` and `main.js`, which your branch also edits. If you change them again before merging, check the merge result.\n\n**Cleanup:** my server and browser tab are closed and my `launch.json` entry is removed. The file now has an empty configurations list, emptied by someone else after my edit, not me. The worktree `/Users/vojta/Dev/protocodus.github.io/.claude/worktrees/hedgerow-grass` is still there, about 330 MB. You can remove it after merging; the branch keeps the commits."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1067,"cache_read_input_tokens":520253,"output_tokens":861,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1067,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":861,"cache_read_input_tokens":520253,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1067,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1067},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"1fd2e623-fb50-481c-ab5d-5a655a8d1627","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CgFSDmpAsDyXmUfuKwzJY","requestRef":"d6c6d4e6-0086-4521-9e1e-31fdf742c572","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","attributionMcpServer":"ccd_turn","attributionMcpTool":"wrap_up","type":"assistant","uuid":"ce2134f1-6670-4be0-99d1-1af9322378c1","timestamp":"2026-10-21T13:09:05.069Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"max","perTurnEffort":"max","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/vojta/Dev/protocodus.github.io/.claude/worktrees/hedgerow-grass","sessionId":"c33bf617-35b